    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d16">

                <pb facs="0031" n="17" sameAs="frus:frus1949v07p1/pg17"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">851G.01/4–249:
                    Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Hanoi</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Gibson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hanoi</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-04-02T14:00:00+08:00">April 2, 1949—2 p.
                            m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>22. Vietminh radio made following announcement: “The High Command of the
                    Vietnamese resistance forces (NB Vietminh) announces that the first elements of
                    the Chinese forces of liberation<anchor n="1" xml:id="d16-f1"/> have registered
                    great activity recently at the Sino-Vietnamese frontier.” Radio then referred to
                    “important support which the Vietnam forces have received as a result.”</p>
                <pb facs="0032" n="18" xml:id="pg18"/>
                <p>This is first official acknowledgment by Vietminh of military cooperation with
                    Chinese.</p>
                <p>Sent Department, repeated Paris 5, pouched Saigon.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Gibson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d16-f1" n="1" xml:id="d16-f1-content">
                <p>Chinese Communist forces under Mao Tse-tung.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
